{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_readme_opencode", "label": "Superpowers for OpenCode README", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/README.opencode.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_readme_opencode_skill_registration", "label": "OpenCode skills directory registration (V1 config hook -> config.skills.paths; V2 setup() -> ctx.skill.transform())", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/README.opencode.md", "source_location": "L124", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registering the skills directory through host-flavor-specific APIs lets OpenCode discover all superpowers skills without symlinks or manual config."}, {"id": "docs_readme_opencode_bootstrap_injection", "label": "OpenCode bootstrap injection (V1 experimental.chat.messages.transform; V2 ctx.session.hook(\"context\"); controller-only, compaction-aware)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/README.opencode.md", "source_location": "L127", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only controller sessions receive the using-superpowers bootstrap as transient model context; delegated child sessions keep native skills but not the bootstrap. After V2 compaction the bootstrap goes into the first retained user message or a transient message after the checkpoint, leaving saved history unchanged. Failed session lookups keep the bootstrap and are not cached."}, {"id": "docs_readme_opencode_tool_mapping", "label": "OpenCode V1/V2 tool mapping (task->subagent, apply_patch->patch, bash->shell, todo dropped in V2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/README.opencode.md", "source_location": "L143", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Skills speak in actions rather than naming any one runtime's tools, so the bootstrap maps them to the tools each OpenCode f